# Family A18: wire envelope layout (internal/wire). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/wire
BENCH=BenchmarkWire
REF=fixed
AUTO_KEY=wire
ADR=18
TITLE="Wire envelope layout (A18)"
# The §10.2 budget cases are BenchmarkWire/<layout>/{Encode,Decode}/1KiB/headers=*
# (≤ 150 / 200 ns, 0 allocs with a caller-owned buffer); size overhead is
# reported per case as overhead-B.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="decode ns/op & 0 allocs with caller buffer -> TLV (forward-compat)"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: internal/wire has no IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX
# branch, and its 18 rows per kind already cross §9.1's {Encode,Decode} with
# {64B,1KiB,64KiB} and the header counts §10.4 asks for.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="Decode Encode 64B 1KiB 64KiB headers=0 headers=4"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op"
